    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27400" root="طى" body-key="T">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَآءٌ</span></b> , also pronounced <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَا</span>, <i>One of the letters of
the alphabet</i> [i. e. <i>the letter</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ط</span>]: masc. and fem.:
Kh says that its <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ا</span> is originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ى</span>. (TA.) [See
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ط</span>.] ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  It is also an epithet applied to a man,
meaning <i>Multum coiens.</i> (KL, TA.)

